          <!-- Section: Why Choose Half-Day -->
          <section id="why-choose-half-day" class="scroll-mt-28 space-y-5">
            <div class="border-l-4 border-amber-500 pl-4 mb-4">
              <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl lg:text-[26px] font-bold text-slate-900 leading-tight">
                Why Choose A Half-Day Cu Chi Tour?
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div class="text-slate-700 text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed space-y-4">
              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. You Get Your Afternoon Back</h3>
              <p>
                The primary advantage of the half-day format is afternoon autonomy. Rather than remaining locked into a guided coach schedule until late afternoon, you return to central Saigon by lunchtime.
              </p>
              <p>
                You can take a leisurely shower, enjoy a relaxed Vietnamese lunch, spend two hours browsing street food and craft stalls near the central market, visit an independent café in the apartment blocks of Nguyen Hue, or book a therapeutic massage. For travelers who value vacation downtime, this balance prevents travel fatigue.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-2">2. It Is Vastly Easier for Families with Young Children</h3>
              <p>
                Managing children through a full 9-to-10 hour touring day in tropical heat is notoriously difficult. The Cu Chi site itself requires navigating unpaved woodland paths, high humidity, outdoor heat, and constant walking.
              </p>
              <p>
                A half-day tour keeps the adventure manageable: kids experience the secret trapdoors and military hardware in the morning and return to the hotel pool before mid-afternoon exhaustion sets in.
              </p>

              <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-2">3. It Maximizes Limited City-Break Time</h3>
              <p>
                If you only have 48 to 72 hours in Ho Chi Minh City, dedicating an entire daylight window to an organized tour consumes half your total stay. A morning excursion lets you experience Cu Chi before noon, leaving your afternoon free to explore vibrant downtown quarters at your own leisure.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

