              <p>
                If you opt for a full-day itinerary, selecting the right companion attractions is crucial. Here is how the top downtown combinations compare:
              </p>

              <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
                <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-xs">
                  <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm sm:text-base mb-1">1. Independence Palace (Reunification Palace)</h3>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    The former presidential palace preserved as it stood on April 30, 1975. It provides the political contrast to Cu Chi's guerrilla tactics. Visitors explore presidential staterooms, the telecommunications war command bunker in the basement, and vintage military hardware on the grounds. Requires approximately 75–90 minutes.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-xs">
                  <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm sm:text-base mb-1">2. War Remnants Museum</h3>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    One of Vietnam's most visited museums, housing heavy military aircraft, artillery, and international photojournalism exhibitions documenting the war's human cost. It deepens historical context but is emotionally intense; families with small children may prefer cultural alternatives.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-xs">
                  <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm sm:text-base mb-1">3. Saigon Central Post Office & French Quarter</h3>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Iconic 19th-century French colonial architecture featuring vaulted ceilings and painted cartography maps. It provides an aesthetic, relaxing contrast after an intensive morning of military history and can easily be enjoyed in 30–45 minutes.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-xs">
                  <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm sm:text-base mb-1">4. Saigon River & Waterbus</h3>
                  <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Cruising the Saigon River provides views of modern skyscrapers contrasting with riverside communities. If using the municipal Waterbus, verify departure schedules in advance. Official guidance requires passengers to check timetables and arrive at the pier prior to departure, with separate ticketing for returns. For an unhurried full-day tour, a chartered private speedboat or evening dinner cruise is often far more predictable than the public commuter ferry.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
